### Page 1 of 22

```text
CHEYENNE REGIONAL AIRPORT BOARD
│BOARD COMMUNICATION COVER MEMORANDUM│

DATE:
May 30, 2024

TO:
The Cheyenne Regional Airport Board

FROM: Jennifer Nelson, Director of Finance

RE:
Consideration and approval of FAA Grant Application No. AIP-069 in the amount of $850,000

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:
For your review and consideration is FAA Grant No. AIP-069, for $850,000 in federal assistance.  This grant
is for the rehabilitation of the tower under the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law (BIL). The federal funds were
granted under the BIL FAA Contract Tower grant application process.  The grant is 100% federally funded
and does not require a state or local match.

The funds from this grant will be used to design and construct the rehabilitation of the Air Traffic Control
Tower (ATCT) at Cheyenne Regional Airport (CYS). The CYS ATCT was originally constructed in 2003.
A building assessment was performed in December, 2021, and it was determined that the building requires
rehabilitation that includes sealing for water intrusion, replacing doors, and other general building repairs.
Additionally, the report identified HVAC and electrical improvements that are required to keep the existing
equipment operational and to improve energy efficiency.
RECOMMENDED ACTION:
Authorize staff to proceed with the grant process, presenting the same information for approval, submission,
and acceptance to the City of Cheyenne and County of Laramie as required signatories.
```

