```text
FAA Form 5100-144 (09/23) SUPERSEDES PREVIOUS EDITION
Page 3 of 5
Program Considerations (Terminal and Tower)
If you check a box below, you must describe how the project satisfies the criteria.
Check all that apply to the proposed project.
Increase Capacity and Passenger Access.  Description (450 Characters Maximum):
Replacing Aging Infrastructure.  Description (450 Characters Maximum):
Achieves Compliance with Americans with Disabilities Act and Expands Accessibility for
Persons with Disabilities.  Description (450 Characters Maximum):
Improves Airport Access for Historically Disadvantaged Populations.
Description (450 Characters Maximum):
Improves Energy Efficiency.  Description (450 Characters Maximum):
The tower is a critical component of CYS's air service and needs to be maintained in order to
provide passengers continued and increased commercial connection. CYS is one of the top
diversion airports for air traffic traveling to DEN. The tower provides an essential services to allow
diversions to occur and enhance safety and operability for the region.
A building assessment (2021) determined that the building requires rehabilitation that includes
sealing for water intrusion, replacing doors and windows, and other general building repairs to
improve personnel safety and overall life expectance of the building. Additionally, HVAC and
electrical improvements are required to keep the existing equipment operational and to improve
energy efficiency.
Minor maintenance will be conducted on the elevator and the associated electrical and
mechanical components to ensure that building maintains ADA compliance. The design will also
look at ways to improve ADA accessibility.
The existing facility has poor energy performance, specifically in HVAC and Electrical
infrastructure.  Building renovations will adhere to LEED standards wherever feasable, in order to
reduce energy consumption, enhance indoor environmental quality, improve resiliency, and
ultimately decrease carbon emmisions to further reduce long-term impacts on the climate.
```

