Maintaining the ATCT is crucial for preserving air service at CYS. The air service pays a key role
in improving the transportation to and from the city, which increases tourism and positively
impacts the local economy.  By having the ATCT, it encourages other potential air carriers to
consider our Airport when expanding air service.
The ATCT is staffed with Air Force Air Traffic Controllers (Squadron 243rd), and is used for
training controllers. The rehabilitation ensures that ATCT personnel can continue to use the
facility, preserving their current good-paying positions and generating additional employment
opportunities as trained personnel transition to other ATCTs for long-term careers. Additionally,
the project will include good-paying jobs for construction.
Operated by Air Force/National Guard (FCT)
